(Machine Learning Primer - Document 2) Tj
T*
T*
(Section 1: Supervised vs Unsupervised Learning) Tj
T*
(Machine learning is categorized into three primary paradigms:) Tj
T*
(1. Supervised Learning: Algorithms are trained on labeled data where inputs are paired with target outputs.) Tj
T*
(Common supervised tasks include classification and linear regression.) Tj
T*
(2. Unsupervised Learning: Algorithms discover hidden patterns, groupings, or clusters in unlabeled data.) Tj
T*
(Prominent unsupervised techniques include k-means clustering and principal component analysis \(PCA\).) Tj
T*
(3. Reinforcement Learning: Agents learn through trial-and-error by interacting with an environment to maximize rewards.) Tj
T*
ET
